## Third-party material

### codebuddy2openai — desensitization word list and technique

- Source: https://github.com/HanHan666666/codebuddy2openai
- File used as reference: `desensitize.py`
- License: MIT
- What was reused: the list of security vocabulary that the upstream content
  filter falsely flags in agent compliance preambles, and the technique of
  inserting a zero-width space (U+200B) inside each matched term to break the
  filter's literal match while keeping the text readable.

The implementation in this repository (`lib/core.js`, the `desensitize*`
functions) is an independent JavaScript rewrite, but the word list is
substantially derived from that project and is credited here accordingly.

## Conceptual precedents

The following projects solve the same general problem (exposing a Tencent
CodeBuddy / WorkBuddy subscription as an OpenAI-compatible API). No code was
taken from them, but they informed the design and are worth knowing about:

- https://github.com/Sliverkiss/workbuddy2api — Go, multi-account gateway
